(6932113, 1045158, 138253, '<td valign="top">love the shadow cast here, great duality of light/dark in a challenge about the end of days.<br/>raised foot gives another layer of imagery/symbolism here that many may miss (not even sure if it was intended).<br/>Great image, lots to see and appreciate here.</td>', 'love the shadow cast here, great duality of light/dark in a challenge about the end of days.raised foot gives another layer of imagery/symbolism here that many may miss (not even sure if it was intended).Great image, lots to see and appreciate here.', '2012-12-14 01:06:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(6932114, 1045148, 138253, '<td valign="top">And they are pondering the last days of man as they float by.<br/>Neitzche had it wrong, it''s when you stare into Clouds that they stare back into you.</td>', 'And they are pondering the last days of man as they float by.Neitzche had it wrong, it''s when you stare into Clouds that they stare back into you.', '2012-12-14 01:06:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(6932116, 1044971, 43463, '<td valign="top">Commenting only not voting yet. <br/> <br/>Ghirahim smirked wickedly, "Until I found these &lt;&lt;Mayan drawings&gt;&gt;, I was....upset about that little stunt the goddess''s guard dog pulled at the Gate of Time. What was that twig''s name again? Impa? Well, never mind that, because these drawings suggest the existence of a second Gate of Time. This news has just filled my heart with rainbows!"<br/> <br/>Ah, another Zelda fan:-) Work on creating Ghirahim is phenominal. Not sure if you can still can this photo-manip as that it has the look of all digital - although I can be wrong as that it is amazing what one can do with photos. Zelda fans may not get the connection of this flamboyant villain to the end of the world if they are not familiar with the game franchise much less Skyward Sword. It might have been best if you had Ghirahim weilding his two swords lunging toward the viewer in a deadly attack...that way both Zelda and non-Zelda (grips heart) people get the concept of ''game over'':-)</td>', 'Commenting only not voting yet.  Ghirahim smirked wickedly, "Until I found these <<Mayan drawings>>, I was....upset about that little stunt the goddess''s guard dog pulled at the Gate of Time. What was that twig''s name again? Impa? Well, never mind that, because these drawings suggest the existence of a second Gate of Time. This news has just filled my heart with rainbows!" Ah, another Zelda fan:-) Work on creating Ghirahim is phenominal. Not sure if you can still can this photo-manip as that it has the look of all digital - although I can be wrong as that it is amazing what one can do with photos. Zelda fans may not get the connection of this flamboyant villain to the end of the world if they are not familiar with the game franchise much less Skyward Sword. It might have been best if you had Ghirahim weilding his two swords lunging toward the viewer in a deadly attack...that way both Zelda and non-Zelda (grips heart) people get the concept of ''game over'':-)', '2012-12-14 01:08:53.000000', NULL, 1),
